uxdroid's change to Dynarmic (azahar-emu/dynarmic a46601580d55, 0BSD; its LICENSE.txt is untouched):
one code cache that every guest CPU of the process shares, so a block is translated once, not once
per guest thread and nesting level. Applied by CMakeLists.txt on top of
docker/translation/dynarmic.patch.

- interface/A64/a64.h, backend/x64/a64_interface.cpp: Jit::Impl is split into CodeCache (the code
  buffer, the emitter and a lock held to look a block up and to emit and link it, never while
  guest code is decoded into IR) and Jit (one CPU's state, which looks in its own fast dispatch
  table before taking the lock when it enters guest code). A cache never clears or invalidates code; with no room
  left it makes the Jit stop with the new HaltReason::CodeCacheFull (interface/halt_reason.h) and
  its owner moves it to another cache with Jit::SetCodeCache. ClearCache and InvalidateCacheRange
  stop the program instead. CodeCache::Translate translates a block ahead of any Jit, and
  CodeCache::Locations lists what a cache translated, for profiles kept between runs. The block
  lookup the dispatcher calls finds the running Jit through a
  thread-local record that each Run saves and restores.
- backend/x64/a64_jitstate.h: what code used to bake in per Jit is in its state, read through r15:
  TPIDR_EL0 and TPIDRRO_EL0 pointers, the fast dispatch table (one per Jit, 1 MiB of lazily
  touched zeros, mapped with mmap), and the exclusive reservation.
- backend/x64/a64_emit_x64.{h,cpp}, emit_x64.{h,cpp}: links between blocks are retargeted with one
  aligned 4- or 8-byte atomic store of a jump displacement or immediate, never rewritten in place,
  so other threads may run the code being linked; the unlinked path is a stub after each location.
- backend/x64/emit_x64.{h,cpp}: the blocks and the jumps waiting for them are one link table
  shared by a cache's emitters, each writing into its own part of one region, under a lock taken
  inside the emitter's; a block registered twice keeps its first copy. a64_emit_x64.cpp records
  no guest ranges, since nothing invalidates by range.
- backend/x64/block_of_code.{h,cpp}: a BlockOfCode can take its memory from a given allocator,
  and the constant pool is not cleared, since fresh mappings are zero.
- backend/x64/emit_x64_memory.cpp.inc: exclusive loads and stores keep the reservation in the
  Jit's state and compare and swap against the value read (the global monitor is ignored, as
  Unsafe_IgnoreGlobalMonitor does); the fastmem fault handler reads its table under a lock of its
  own and never recompiles a block.

